## Program Outcome

Tool Shed website and dashboard changes are developed and proven on a private, production-like
site before intentional public promotion. The development stack is isolated from production on
the shared `sup.local` Docker host, is reachable only from approved LAN clients and a Workpc
localhost tunnel, communicates continuously with dedicated Linux and Windows development project
identities, and supports exact-commit promotion with recovery evidence.

## M1-ISOLATED-PRIVATE-DEVELOPMENT — Establish the development target

Status: planned
Required Endpoint: Work2 to a verified split development target
Depends on: none

Outcome: Create and verify the separate development filesystem and Compose project, independent
services and writable resources, plain-HTTP LAN endpoint on port `8443`, synthetic seed data,
resource limits, unmistakable environment identity, LAN test-bed access, and persistent
localhost-only Workpc tunnel. Production remains healthy and unchanged.

Gates:

- `G1-DEVELOPMENT-ISOLATION`
- `G3-PRIVATE-ACCESS`

Candidate campaign: `establish-isolated-private-development-site`.

Execution boundary: the current `combined` Work2 target must not be used for bootstrap. First bind
the exact development root and deployment commands, keep every Compose operation scoped to the
development project, and retain the combined declaration until the new target is actually healthy.
Development-secret or authentication creation remains an explicit protected boundary.

## M2-DEVELOPMENT-COMMUNICATION — Exercise the real development integration

Status: planned
Required Endpoint: Work2 to the verified development target and both dedicated test-bed identities
Depends on: M1-ISOLATED-PRIVATE-DEVELOPMENT

Outcome: Dedicated Linux and Windows development project identities enroll with development-only
credentials, complete one manual report handshake, then operate persistent reporter workers and
safety schedulers against the development dashboard. Reports and bounded telemetry converge
without redirecting or reusing a production-connected identity.

Gate:

- `G2-DEVELOPMENT-COMMUNICATION`

Candidate campaign: `connect-dedicated-development-reporters`.

Execution boundary: credential issuance, TOTP/authentication changes, and host-local scheduler
installation require explicit protected authority at the time of action. Production reporter
state, queues, credentials, and destinations remain untouched.

## M3-PROMOTION-AND-RECOVERY-PROOF — Prove the public promotion path

Status: planned
Required Endpoint: Work5 for one explicitly selected development-tested commit
Depends on: M1-ISOLATED-PRIVATE-DEVELOPMENT, M2-DEVELOPMENT-COMMUNICATION

Outcome: Prove migrations and recovery on non-production data; pass login, MFA, dashboard,
enrollment, Linux, Windows, and Workpc checks; confirm development has no public route; back up
production before any migration-bearing promotion; promote the exact tested commit; and verify
production health and a practical rollback path.

Gate:

- `G4-PROMOTION-RECOVERY`

Candidate campaign: `qualify-and-promote-development-tested-commit`.

Execution boundary: this roadmap does not itself authorize a production release. M3 starts only
from an explicit Work5 request naming or unambiguously selecting the tested candidate and after
protected production controls, backup, and rollback readiness are satisfied.

